From 27c93938da290e11e28adfd28509abeaee93bb4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 14:56:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] vulkan: enable mask-opt for QSA decode (nem1 == 1) in
 flash attention

The use_mask_opt gate required nem1 >= 32, so the QSA decode path (single
query row) never used the block-skip scan even at long contexts where the
top-k mask leaves most KV cells fully masked. The coopmat2 shader already
skips all-NEG-INF blocks when built with mask opt.

Measured on gfx1151 (FP2MIX v2, KV q8_0): combined16k +8.2%
(186.69 -> 202.04 t/s), combined32k +0.9%, tg512 unchanged; ppl identical
to the 4th decimal (skip of fully-masked blocks is exact by construction);
battery probe fidelity 12/12 PASS.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index 782f2f626..56a296c56 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -10372,7 +10372,10 @@ static void ggml_vk_flash_attn(ggml_backend_vk_context * ctx, vk_context& subctx
     }
 
     // Only use mask opt when the mask is fairly large. This hasn't been tuned extensively.
-    bool use_mask_opt = mask && nem1 >= 32 && nem0 * nem1 > 32768 && nem0 >= tuning_params.block_cols * 16;
+    // QSA decode (nem1 == 1): the top-k mask leaves most KV cells fully masked at long
+    // contexts — the mask-opt scan pass lets the shader skip whole masked blocks.
+    bool use_mask_opt = mask && ((nem1 >= 32 && nem0 * nem1 > 32768 && nem0 >= tuning_params.block_cols * 16) ||
+                                 (nem1 == 1 && nem0 >= 8192));
     vk_fa_pipeline_state fa_pipeline_state = get_fa_pipeline_state(ctx->device, tuning_params, HSK, HSV, aligned, f32acc,
                                                                    mask != nullptr, use_mask_opt, logit_softcap != 0, k_fa_type, v_fa_type);
 
